{"entity":{"id":"hb:taiwan@1878","name":"Taiwan","dataset":"basemaps","kind":"polity"},"territories":[{"id":8176,"name":"Taiwan","set_id":"hb_1878","class":"polity","valid_from":1878,"valid_to":1880,"snapshot_held":1,"area_km2":36105.04121659152,"border_precision":3,"capital_name":null,"sovereign":null,"sovereign_note":null,"modern_name":"Taiwan","min_lon":120.049149,"min_lat":21.92777300000012,"max_lon":122.002213,"max_lat":25.284164,"source_file":"world_1878.geojson","source_row":null},{"id":8352,"name":"Taiwan","set_id":"hb_1880","class":"polity","valid_from":1880,"valid_to":1900,"snapshot_held":1,"area_km2":36105.04121659173,"border_precision":3,"capital_name":null,"sovereign":null,"sovereign_note":null,"modern_name":"Taiwan","min_lon":120.049149,"min_lat":21.927773000000116,"max_lon":122.002213,"max_lat":25.284164,"source_file":"world_1880.geojson","source_row":null}],"identities":[{"qid":"Q319881","from_t":1895.2904109589042,"to_t":1895.8027397260273,"method":"name-template+date","confidence":0.9340620618687794,"label":"Republic of Formosa","description":"republic created to resist Japanese occupation","inception":1895.3945205479451,"dissolved":1895.8027397260273,"enwiki":"Republic of Formosa","summary":"The Republic of Formosa was a short-lived unrecognized state that existed on the island of Taiwan in 1895 during the interregnum between the formal cession of Taiwan by the Qing dynasty of China to the Empire of Japan after the Treaty of Shimonoseki. The Republic lasted for 151 days; it was proclaimed on 23 May 1895 and extinguished on 21 October, when its capital of Tainan was taken over by the Japanese and they established control on the island."},{"qid":"Q137816","from_t":1895.8027397260273,"to_t":1900,"method":"name-alias+date","confidence":0.8165781755119321,"label":"Taiwan under Japanese rule","description":"period of Taiwanese history (1895–1945)","inception":1895.2904109589042,"dissolved":1945,"enwiki":"Taiwan under Japanese rule","summary":"The island of Taiwan, along with the Penghu Islands, became an annexed territory of the Empire of Japan in 1895, when the Qing dynasty ceded Fujian-Taiwan Province in the Treaty of Shimonoseki after the Japanese victory in the First Sino-Japanese War. After Japanese forces crushed the consequent Republic of Formosa resistance movement, Japan ruled Taiwan for 50 years. Its capital was located in Taihoku (Taipei), the seat of the Governor-General of Taiwan.\nTaiwan was Japan's first colony and can be viewed as the first step in implementing their \"Southern Expansion Doctrine\" of the late 19th century."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q319881","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q701499","value_label":"Tang Jingsong","from_t":1895.3287671232877,"to_t":1895.4136986301369,"title":"head of state","property":"P35","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Tang Jingsong"},{"qid":"Q319881","kind":"ruler","value_qid":"Q709550","value_label":"Liu Yongfu","from_t":1895.4136986301369,"to_t":1985.7479452054795,"title":"head of state","property":"P35","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Liu Yongfu"},{"qid":"Q319881","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q15935383","value_label":"Taipei Prefecture","from_t":1895.3945205479451,"to_t":1895.4136986301369,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Taipei Prefecture"},{"qid":"Q319881","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q16078002","value_label":"Tainan Prefecture","from_t":1895.4136986301369,"to_t":1895.7479452054795,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Tainan Prefecture"},{"qid":"Q319881","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q9192","value_label":"Mandarin","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Mandarin"},{"qid":"Q319881","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q36778","value_label":"Taiwanese Hokkien","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Taiwanese Hokkien"},{"qid":"Q319881","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q33375","value_label":"Hakka Chinese","